    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d898">

                <pb facs="1126" n="1112" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg1112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24596/4–2947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the Philippines
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u.s. urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-19T19:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>582. You many inform Roxas that although Article 13<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d898-f1"/> gives United States exclusive jurisdiction “in time of
                    war” and United States is now legally at war this Government has no intention of
                    claiming such jurisdiction as it was not understanding of parties to agreement
                    that Article 13(6) should apply during present war.</p>
                <p>Dept does not consider that this has any bearing on or is a precedent for lease
                    case mentioned your 687, Apr. 29<anchor n="19" xml:id="d898-f2"/> since question
                    in that case is what was intention of parties to lease contract.</p>
                <p>Pass to Army and Navy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d898-f1" n="18" xml:id="d898-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is to the agreement on military bases signed March 14.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d898-f2" n="19" xml:id="d898-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
